WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.531 --> 00:00:06.560
Speaker 1: And while we're on the topic of&nbsp;
election lies, let's talk about Lin Wood for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:12.320
a moment. The Trump loving lawyer recently&nbsp;
got smacked down in an embarrassing way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:19.280
by yet another court over his bogus&nbsp;
election fraud claims. Now, Lynwood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:26.960
I'm sorry he's such a comical character. If he&nbsp;
weren't so, you know, obviously whatever. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:35.120
anyway, Lin Wood goes out December of last year,&nbsp;
files multiple different lawsuits alleging fraud.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:40.080
But the main ones he filed were in the state of&nbsp;
Georgia, where he had two separate lawsuits going,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:45.200
one challenging the results of Georgia's&nbsp;
presidential election. The other one actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:52.000
came a little later in January, challenging the&nbsp;
Senate election. And in that challenge, which the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.280
first won, the election challenge in general was&nbsp;
thrown out, said it was baseless. The other one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:04.720
got thrown out for a second time by the Court of&nbsp;
Appeals late last week because they said that Lin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:11.680
Wood, you have no standing in this case. So here's&nbsp;
what Lin Wood was actually challenging here, Wood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:17.760
came out and said that because they change the&nbsp;
rules, the state changed the rules for signature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.400
verification. The whole thing is fraudulent and&nbsp;
you cannot trust it. They didn't have the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:31.360
signature verification. For the absentee&nbsp;
ballots that were obviously very prevalent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.040
in that Georgia runoff election, so&nbsp;
the first court that looked at this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.960
way, way, way back in early this year said,&nbsp;
yeah, you don't have standing to say any of this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:50.560
The state legislature controlled by Republicans,&nbsp;
passed a law that gave their Republican secretary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:56.000
of state, Brad Raffensperger, the ability&nbsp;
to change the rules for the absentee ballots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.680
because it was in the middle of a pandemic, they&nbsp;
knew they were going to have a lot of absentee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.080
ballots. They were counting on it. That is what&nbsp;
their election was basically going to have to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:09.440
because of the pandemic. He had the authority to&nbsp;
do this, the authority given to him by the state.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:17.040
You therefore have no standing, Lin Wood and the&nbsp;
Court of Appeals last week basically told him the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:24.400
exact same thing. You have no injury. You have no&nbsp;
actual claim of illegal activity, again, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:29.920
he was given the authority to do this. States,&nbsp;
as we all know, have the authority to determine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:36.560
how their own elections are run without the&nbsp;
interference of outside forces. So, no, Mr. Wood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:41.200
you don't get to come into these courts&nbsp;
and tell us that something illegal happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:47.040
when all of the changes that you're actually&nbsp;
challenging were approved by the state.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:59.520
No injury, no illegal activity, no standing for&nbsp;
Mr. Lin Wood, I don't know how many total court&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:04.880
losses this brings us to at this point with people&nbsp;
like Lin Wood and Giuliani and Sidney Powell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:10.880
But I can promise you they're going to continue&nbsp;
to lose. But of course, that hasn't stopped the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:16.320
Republicans in all these states where the lawsuits&nbsp;
are losing from an acting, these highly oppressive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:22.960
and repressive voting laws. So that, I guess,&nbsp;
is the silver lining for Republicans. You may be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:29.840
losing the court battles, but you've won the war&nbsp;
on voter suppression. For now, we have to take a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:35.200
quick break. I'm Ferring Cousins from Ring of Fire&nbsp;
sitting in for David Pakman. We'll be right back.

